.TH CUPSD 8 "2026-11-18" "yindle 0.1.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
cupsd \- Yindle CUPS-compatible print scheduler and IPP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cupsd
.RB [ \-c
.IR cupsd.conf ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR cups\-files.conf ]
.RB [ \-f | \-F ]
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-format
.IR text | json ]
.br
.B cupsd
.B \-\-check\-config
.RB [ \-c
.IR cupsd.conf ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR cups\-files.conf ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B cupsd
.B doctor
.RB [ \-c
.IR cupsd.conf ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR cups\-files.conf ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B cupsd
.RB [ \-v | \-V | \-\-version ]
.br
.B cupsd
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cupsd
is the Yindle print scheduler, a memory-safe Rust drop-in replacement for the
OpenPrinting CUPS 2.x daemon.
It implements the Internet Printing Protocol (IPP 1.0\(en2.2 and IPP Everywhere),
HTTP/1.1 with RFC 2817 TLS upgrade and direct TLS/mTLS listeners, Unix domain
socket peer authentication
.RB ( SO_PEERCRED ),
PAM-first Basic authentication, fail-closed
.B <Location>
and
.B <Policy>
authorization, driverless and PPD/filter-based job pipelines sandboxed via
.BR cups\-exec ,
DNS-SD/AirPrint advertising, D-Bus notifications, and built-in HTTP observability
endpoints.
.PP
Existing CUPS configuration files
.RB ( cupsd.conf (5),
.BR cups\-files.conf (5),
.IR printers.conf ,
.IR classes.conf ,
.IR subscriptions.conf ),
the
.I /var/spool/cups
layout, and external filters/backends work in place.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " cupsd.conf"
Use an alternate
.B cupsd.conf
configuration file instead of the default
.IR /etc/cups/cupsd.conf .
.TP
.BI \-s " cups\-files.conf"
Use an alternate
.B cups\-files.conf
configuration file instead of resolving a sibling
.I cups\-files.conf
next to
.I cupsd.conf
or
.IR /etc/cups/cups\-files.conf .
Honored even when combined with
.BR \-c .
.TP
.B \-f
Run
.B cupsd
in the foreground rather than detaching to the background (recommended for
containers and process supervisors).
.TP
.B \-F
Run
.B cupsd
in the foreground without detaching from the controlling terminal or process
group.
.TP
.B \-l
Run in on-demand / socket-activated mode (used by
.IR cups.service ),
exiting cleanly when idle for
.B IdleExitTimeout
seconds with no active jobs, clients, or subscriptions.
.TP
.B \-t
Test the configuration files for syntax errors, print diagnostics, and exit
without starting the scheduler.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-V ", " \-\-version
Print Yindle version information and exit with status 0.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit with status 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-format " text|json"
Select log output format for
.IR error_log ,
.IR access_log ,
.IR page_log ,
and audit events.
Defaults to classic CUPS
.B text
format.
Set
.B json
(or the environment variable
.BR YINDLE_LOG_FORMAT=json )
for newline-delimited structured JSON suitable for SIEM/ELK/Loki ingestion.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-config " [" \-\-json ]
Run the built-in configuration migration and security linter against
.I cupsd.conf
and
.IR cups\-files.conf .
Classifies every directive as Supported, Deprecated, Moved, or Unknown, and
reports security findings (such as
.BR FILE_DEVICE_ENABLED ,
.BR LOCATION_SATISFY_ANY ,
.BR WILDCARD_LISTEN ,
.BR WILDCARD_SERVER_ALIAS ,
or
.BR WEAK_TLS_OPTIONS )
with remediation hints.
Exits non-zero on parse errors.
Pass
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.TP
.BR doctor " [" \-c " " \fIcupsd.conf\fP "] [" \-s " " \fIcups\-files.conf\fP "] [" \-\-json ]
Run live host and environment readiness diagnostics: checks configuration syntax
and security posture, required directory existence and permissions
.RB ( ServerRoot ,
.BR RequestRoot ,
.BR CacheDir ,
.BR TempDir ,
.BR LogDir ,
.BR StateDir ),
loaded MIME rule counts, presence and permissions of
.BR cups\-exec ,
.BR cups\-deviced ,
.BR cups\-driverd ,
backends, and filters, TLS certificate/key validity, PAM/NSS availability, and
known host conflicts (such as a leftover stock Ubuntu/Debian AppArmor profile
at
.IR /etc/apparmor.d/usr.sbin.cupsd ).
.SH HTTP OBSERVABILITY AND STATUS ENDPOINTS
Subject to configured
.B <Location>
rules,
.B cupsd
exposes built-in operational endpoints alongside IPP:
.TP
.B GET /healthz
Liveness endpoint returning HTTP 200 JSON with scheduler status, version, and
uptime.
.TP
.B GET /readyz
Readiness endpoint returning HTTP 200 JSON when the spooler and scheduler are
ready, or HTTP 503 Service Unavailable while draining or unhealthy.
.TP
.B GET /metrics
Prometheus text exposition
.RB ( text/plain;\ version=0.0.4;\ charset=utf\-8 )
exporting
.BR yindle_jobs_active ,
.BR yindle_jobs_pending ,
.BR yindle_jobs_total ,
.BR yindle_job_duration_seconds ,
.BR yindle_ipp_requests_total ,
.BR yindle_auth_failures_total ,
.BR yindle_active_clients ,
.BR yindle_filter_cost_current ,
and
.BR yindle_filter_limit .
.TP
.BR "GET /" ", " /printers ", " /classes ", " /jobs
When
.B WebInterface Yes
is enabled and no static files or stock CGI scripts exist in
.BR DocumentRoot ,
serves a built-in, read-only, XSS-escaped HTML status interface with security
headers
.RB ( X\-Content\-Type\-Options ,
.BR X\-Frame\-Options ,
.BR Content\-Security\-Policy ).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Zero-downtime configuration reload: notifies systemd
.RB ( RELOADING=1 ),
reloads
.I cupsd.conf
and
.IR cups\-files.conf ,
reloads the MIME database, atomically reloads TLS certificates and keys from
.B ServerKeychain
(retaining the previous valid certificate on error), reopens log files for
.BR logrotate (8),
refreshes DNS-SD advertisements, and notifies systemd
.RB ( READY=1 ).
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown: notifies systemd
.RB ( STOPPING=1 ),
switches
.B /readyz
to HTTP 503, stops accepting new connections, deregisters DNS-SD services,
drains in-flight requests, terminates active job process groups cleanly, and
persists
.IR printers.conf ,
.IR classes.conf ,
.IR subscriptions.conf ,
and
.I job.cache
before exiting.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YINDLE_LOG_FORMAT
Set to
.B json
or
.B text
to choose the default log format when
.B \-\-log\-format
is not passed on the command line.
.TP
.BR LISTEN_FDS ", " LISTEN_PID
Standard systemd socket-activation variables consumed via
.B sd_listen_fds
(file descriptors are marked
.B FD_CLOEXEC
and variables are cleared before spawning children).
.TP
.BR NOTIFY_SOCKET ", " WATCHDOG_USEC
Standard systemd readiness, reload, stop, and watchdog notification variables.
.TP
.B TZ
POSIX time zone or zoneinfo identifier used by Yindle's thread-safe pure-Rust
RFC 8536 TZif localtime log formatter.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cups/cupsd.conf
Primary scheduler configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/cups/cups\-files.conf
Filesystem paths, permissions, user/group, and sandboxing configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/cups/printers.conf
Persisted printer queue definitions (mode 0640, root:lp).
.TP
.I /etc/cups/classes.conf
Persisted printer class definitions (mode 0640, root:lp).
.TP
.I /etc/cups/subscriptions.conf
Persisted RFC 3995 event subscriptions (mode 0640, root:lp).
.TP
.I /etc/cups/ppd/
Per-queue PPD files.
.TP
.I /etc/cups/ssl/
TLS server certificate
.RI ( server.crt )
and private key
.RI ( server.key ,
directory mode 0700, key mode 0600).
.TP
.I /usr/share/cups/mime/
Standard MIME type and conversion rule database
.RI ( mime.types ", " mime.convs ).
.TP
.I /var/spool/cups/
Job control
.RI ( c* )
and document
.RI ( d* )
spool files (mode 0600, lp:lp).
.TP
.I /var/log/cups/
Scheduler log files
.RI ( error_log ", " access_log ", " page_log ).
.TP
.I /run/cups/cups.sock
Local Unix domain socket for IPP clients and
.B SO_PEERCRED
authentication.
.SH SECURITY
Yindle enforces
.B #![forbid(unsafe_code)]
across all crates outside one audited FFI crate, defaults
.B <Location>
and
.B <Policy>
blocks to fail-closed
.BR "Satisfy all" ,
binds
.I cups.socket
to loopback by default, drops filter/backend privileges via
.B cups\-exec
with
.BR "umask 077" ,
.BR setrlimit (2),
.BR PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS ,
and Linux Landlock sandboxing, and enforces outbound backend SSRF protections.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination, valid configuration test, or passing diagnostics.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal startup error, invalid command-line arguments, failed configuration test,
or failing diagnostics.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate configuration syntax and run security/migration audit:
.PP
.EX
sudo cupsd \-t
sudo cupsd \-\-check\-config
sudo cupsd doctor
.EE
.PP
Run an isolated unprivileged instance on port 8631 with structured JSON logs:
.PP
.EX
cupsd \-c /tmp/pw/etc/cupsd.conf \-s /tmp/pw/etc/cups\-files.conf \-f \-\-log\-format json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cupsd.conf (5),
.BR cups\-files.conf (5),
.BR cups\-lpd (8),
.BR cupsfilter (8),
.BR lpadmin (8),
.BR lpstat (1),
